                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+theorem+for+monoidal+categories"} coherence theorem for monoidal categories
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
                  %p
                    %strong In higher category theory
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+2-category"} monoidal 2-category
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+2-category"} braided monoidal 2-category
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+bicategory"} monoidal bicategory
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+bicategory"} cartesian bicategory
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} k-tuply monoidal n-category
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+cubes+operad"} little cubes operad
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} monoidal (∞,1)-category
                      %ul
                        %li
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+double+category"} compact double category
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %em Bénabou cosmos
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            with good properties that make it a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+of+enrichment"} base of enrichment
            well-suited for
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"} cosmos
            for more).
          %p
            The archetypical Bénabou cosmos is the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            of all sets, equipped with its
            = succeed "-monoidal" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            is the ordinary theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+categories"} locally small categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
          %p
            The point of the notion of Bénabou cosmoi is to allow more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-objects"} hom-objects
            than just
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            which these form in order that most standard definitions and proofs of plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            (e.g. properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+categories"} enriched functor categories
            and specifically of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+presheaves"} categories of presheaves
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+presheaves"} enriched presheaves
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #BenabouCosmosAccordingToStreet.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9nabou+cosmos"} Bénabou cosmos
              is (
              %a{:href => "#Street74"}> Street 74, p. 1
              ) a
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
                  (hence
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicomplete+category"} bicomplete
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              (cf
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+closed+category"} symmetric monoidal closed category
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              There is a generalization of Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BenabouCosmosAccordingToStreet"}
              to the context of enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+categories"} indexed categories
              (
              %a{:href => "#Shulman13"}> Shulman 2013
              ). While Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BenabouCosmosAccordingToStreet"}
              is not “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"}> elementary
              ” (as it involves infinitary (non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"}> finite
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              and
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %em is
              elementary, as the infinitary structure is folded into the indexing base category. The notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9nabou+cosmoi"} Bénabou cosmoi
              is recovered as particular indexed cosmoi over
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %p
          #TopoiAreCosmoi.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topoi"} topoi
                are
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmoi"} cosmoi
              %br/
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
              is a Bénabou cosmos, where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
              structure is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The archetypical such example is the category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Set
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
                  are ordinary
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+categories"} locally small categories
              %li
                %p
                  The category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
                  over the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products+of+simplicial+sets"} products of simplicial sets
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi sSet
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
                  are often called
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+categories"} simplicial categories
                  (though see there for ambiguity in this terminology). They serve as foundation for much of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial homotopy theory
                  and
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+categories"} simplicial model categories
                  for more.
            %p
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"}> cosmos
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+of+enrichment"} base of enrichment
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-cosmos"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  \-cosmos
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Apparently there is no explicit written account by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"} Jean Bénabou
            on the notion, but one finds it recounted in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Street74"} Street 74, p. 1
          %blockquote
            %p
              to J. Benabou the word means “bicomplete symmetric monoidal category”, such categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              being rich enough so that the theory of categories enriched in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              develops to a large extent just as the theory of ordinary categories.
          %ul
            %li#Street74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              ,
              %em Elementary cosmoi I.
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %em Category Seminar
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 420
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0063103"} doi:10.1007/BFb0063103
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmos_(th%C3%A9orie_des_cat%C3%A9gories)"} Cosmos_(théorie_des_catégories)
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} indexed
            generalization:
          %ul
            %li#Shulman13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Enriched indexed categories
              %strong 28
              21 (2013) 616-695 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/28/21/28-21abs.html"}> tac:28-21
              )
